From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: apple-soc: wait for a transition before an
 idle drop by default

On a J604 at idle, with idle_drop_wait flipped at runtime for 10 s each
way, the P cluster sat at its top state in 4.2 % of samples instead of
27.8 %; its rail drew 289 mW instead of 812 mW and the whole machine
9.07 W instead of 9.82 W. Of 3333 drops that found a transition in
flight, 24 still gave up waiting. After one suspend-to-idle cycle the
rail drew 325 mW, with the display, the GPU and the network working.

Make it the default. idle_drop_wait stays writable at runtime as the
way back to the old behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
index 4ef9eeaf28..cd638eee19 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
@@ -559,10 +559,10 @@ static int apple_soc_cpufreq_set_pstate(struct apple_cpu_priv *priv,
  * cluster's next wake, a few milliseconds at most.
  *
  * A wake shorter than a transition finds the restore it asked for still in
- * flight when its CPU goes idle again. By default the drop is then skipped,
- * which leaves the cluster at its top state for the whole idle; with
- * idle_drop_wait it waits for that transition (APPLE_DVFS_IDLE_WAIT_US at
- * most) instead. Both cases are counted in dvfs_registers.
+ * flight when its CPU goes idle again. With idle_drop_wait (the default) the
+ * drop waits for that transition (APPLE_DVFS_IDLE_WAIT_US at most); without
+ * it the drop is skipped, which leaves the cluster at its top state for the
+ * whole idle. Both cases are counted in dvfs_registers.
  *
  * Only the clusters of the fastest cores take part: the J604's E cluster
  * costs about 20 mW at its top state, not worth slower wakes for the
@@ -572,9 +572,9 @@ static bool idle_drop = true;
 module_param(idle_drop, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(idle_drop, "T8132: while every CPU of the performance cluster waits in a long idle, run the cluster at its slowest P-state and restore the governor's state on the first wake (default: on)");
 
-static bool idle_drop_wait;
+static bool idle_drop_wait = true;
 module_param(idle_drop_wait, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(idle_drop_wait, "T8132: when the cluster is still changing state as its last CPU goes idle, wait for the transition (at most 100 us) and drop the cluster, instead of leaving it at its state for that idle (default: off)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(idle_drop_wait, "T8132: when the cluster is still changing state as its last CPU goes idle, wait for the transition (at most 100 us) and drop the cluster, instead of leaving it at its state for that idle (default: on)");
 
 static DEFINE_PER_CPU(struct apple_cpu_priv *, apple_idle_priv);
 
